      en: "The Płock Refinery, owned by energy giant PKN Orlen, is the largest oil refinery in Poland and one of the most complex and modern facilities of its kind in Europe. Located on the banks of the Vistula River, the refinery is a cornerstone of Poland's energy security, processing a significant portion of the country's crude oil. It is connected to Russian oil via the Druzhba pipeline and to seaborne imports via the Port of Gdańsk. The facility produces a wide range of fuels, including gasoline, diesel, and jet fuel, as well as a variety of petrochemicals used in the plastics and chemical industries. Ongoing investments in technology and sustainability aim to increase its efficiency and reduce its environmental footprint.",
